1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,399
This is the very cute model village which is a tiny bourton on the water replica.
这就是那个非常可爱的模型村，是水上伯顿村的微缩复制品。

2
00:00:05,399 --> 00:00:15,230
The attention to detail here is really quite something there's even a model village within the model village and within that model village is another model village.
这里对细节的用心，确实很了不起。模型村里面甚至还有一个模型村，而那个模型村里，又有一个模型村。

3
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:26,160
It's even built using the same cotswold stone as its inspiration chieki actually came here as a child and we recreated that special moment with some success.
它甚至使用与原村庄相同的科茨沃尔德石材建造。我的同行者小时候其实来过这里，我们也算是成功重现了当年的那个特别时刻。

4
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:04,279
Something that we kept stumbling upon were these traditional red telephone boxes that had been converted to defibrillators.
我们一路上不断偶遇这些传统红色电话亭，它们已经被改造成了放置除颤器的设施。

5
00:01:04,279 --> 00:01:14,720
I later learned that this particular one in lower slaughter was actually the first in the country to be used for this purpose turning an unused kiosk into something potentially life saving.
后来我得知，位于 Lower Slaughter 的这一个，据说是全国首个用于这种用途的电话亭，把一个废弃的电话亭，变成可能救人一命的设施。

6
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:38,510
Wandering around upper slaughter we stumbled on this hotel and nearing lunch time we took the opportunity to order a cream tea with this picturesque view.
在 Upper Slaughter 四处闲逛时，我们偶然发现了这家酒店。那时快到午饭时间，我们便趁机点了一份奶油茶，欣赏眼前如画的风景。

7
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:46,300
Now I'm still not sure if my jam is supposed to go on top of the cream or it's the other way around so I just always like to hedge my bets.
到现在，我还是不确定果酱应该放在奶油上面，还是反过来。所以我总喜欢两种方式都试试，免得选错。

8
00:02:36,679 --> 00:02:42,400
This is arlington row in bibury the most photographed street in the cotswolds.
这是 Bibury 的 Arlington Row；作者称它是科茨沃尔德被拍照最多的街道。

9
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:51,310
Originally built in the 14 th century as a store selling wool it was converted to cottages 300 years later.
据作者介绍，这里最初建于十四世纪，用作售卖羊毛的店铺，三百年后被改成了小屋。

10
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:57,710
If it seems familiar to some of you it's because it's on the very first page of your british passport.
如果一些英国观众觉得眼熟，那是因为作者说，它就出现在英国护照的第一页。

11
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:05,359
People do live here remember so it is a bit odd with everyone taking photos but you can actually book a stay in number 9.
别忘了，这里确实有人居住，所以大家都来拍照，感觉有点奇怪，不过你也可以预订九号小屋住一晚。

12
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:15,640
Nosying around on their website gives you the chance to see the inside of these lovely cottages just be aware that there will be zero welcoming of dogs.
在他们的网站上四处看看，就有机会看到这些可爱小屋的内部。只是要注意，作者当时查到的规定，是完全不欢迎带狗入住。

13
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:26,990
Another quick run in the car took us to cirencester often referred to as the capital of the cotswolds.
又开了一小段路，我们到了 Cirencester，人们常把它称作科茨沃尔德的首府。

14
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,590
This would be the only city we would be visiting so found ourselves mostly just browsing all the shops.
这是作者说他们这趟唯一会去的“城市”，所以我们大多时候都只是在各家商店里逛逛。

15
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:38,440
Following a quick look of how much it would cost to move here we made our way home for some rest and relaxation.
匆匆了解了一下搬来这里要花多少钱后，我们就回住处休息放松了，

16
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:43,780
As tomorrow we'd be embarking on our very first cotswolds hike.
因为第二天，我们将要开始第一次科茨沃尔德徒步。
